   "scope": "Target-genre items only. A span is gold when a finite passive clause names no doer and its verb reports (a) a fault or wrongful act, (b) unauthorised access to, acquisition of or disclosure of data the speaking body held, (c) concealment or restriction of information, or (d) a vague remedial claim ('steps will be taken', 'action was taken', 'it is put right'). Not gold: negated non-events ('has not been affected'), detection and investigation ('was discovered'), concrete remedies ('were deactivated', 'have been removed'), routine procedure, statives, reduced (non-finite) participles, and clauses whose doer is named ('by the High Court'). The span runs from the first auxiliary through the participle.",
   "note": "Annotated from the item text alone, before any detector was run on these items. The annotator had read packages/rules-en/rules.json, spec/taxonomy.yaml and the agentless-passive detector, so this gold is not blind."
